  "id": "DrugBank_DB01234 - MONDO_2970",
  "verbalization": "Dexamethasone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Ciliary Body Disease through a series of indirect pathways involving corticosteroids. The evidence suggests that Dexamethasone, through its indication for Panuveitis and Iris Disease, may influence the development of Ciliary Body Disease via mechanisms that involve inflammation and cellular dysfunction. The presence of multiple corticosteroids—such as Rimexolone and Fluorometholone—linked to Ciliary Body Disease further supports the notion that corticosteroid use could contribute to this condition. While the direct causal link between Dexamethasone and Ciliary Body Disease remains unclear, the shared pathway through Panuveitis and the indirect relationship with corticosteroids provide a coherent framework for understanding the potential role of Dexamethasone in this disease. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of corticosteroid use in inflammatory conditions, suggesting a possible mechanistic link that warrants further investigation.",
